Figure~\ref{fig1} presents the ratios of prompt and non-prompt D-meson production cross sections measured in pp collisions at $\sqrt{s}$ = 5.02 and 13 TeV~\cite{2,4}. These results are compared with theoretical calculations based on pQCD: FONLL~\cite{1} for prompt D mesons and a combination of FONLL with PYTHIA 8~\cite{3} for non-prompt D mesons.  The ratios are consistent for both prompt and non-prompt D mesons, and the data are well described by FONLL calculations, which rely on quark fragmentation functions extracted from $\rm e^{+} e^{-}$ and ep collisions. This supports the assumption of universality of fragmentation functions for mesons. The results are also compatible at different center-of-mass energies.

\subsection{Baryon-to-meson ratio}
