We run the test for a set of strikes $K \in [50, 55, 60, 65, 70, 75, 80]$. The previously computed value $y(t_{i-1})$ is used as the initial guess, and the iterative method typically converges within 3-4 iterations. The computational efficiency is noteworthy: computing $S_B(t)$ on a temporal grid $t_i = i\Delta t$, $i \in \{0, 1, \ldots, M\}$, $\Delta t = T/M$ for all strikes with $M = 20$ requires only 0.33 seconds in MATLAB on a system with two Intel Quad-Core i7-4790 CPUs at 3.80 GHz. While this MATLAB implementation could be naturally vectorized for improved performance, we have not pursued this optimization since our focus is on demonstrating the basic methodology, which can be enhanced in various ways as discussed in \cite{ItkinMuravey2024jd}.

