    (a,c) Degree heterogeneity index $\eta_k$ versus RG steps $\ell$, with errorbars denoting standard deviations.     (b,d) Degree distribution $P(k)$ at various RG steps $\ell$. In (b), RN and BA converge to  similar Poissonian forms at large $\ell$, while in (d), ER hypergraphs develop power-law behavior  at $\ell=10$ and $20$; a dotted line with slope $-4$ is shown as a visual guide. 
