So far, microwave shielding has been restricted to gases composed of a single internal state. In the fermionic system, collisions occur primarily via $p$-wave channels.
%, limiting the tunability of the interaction and the evaporative cooling efficiency.
While enhanced $p$-wave interactions have recently been demonstrated by tuning to a field-linked resonance (FLR) \cite{Chen:2023}, this required a highly elliptical field polarization, which compromises the shielding efficiency and thereby the stability of the sample \cite{Karman:2019}. The fermionic systems with the lowest entropy ($T/T_F\simeq0.36$ \cite{Schindewolf:2022}, where $T_F$ is the Fermi temperature) have therefore been prepared far away from an FLR.

