In the \cite{Gil_Mar_n_2012} approach, the oscillations in $n$ due to the BAO are removed. To do so,  we simply interpolate $n(k)$ through the mean. To find the mean, we locate the extrema of the oscillations and define interpolating nodes at middle between the extrema (in $\ln k$). 


