\subsection{Halo Bias}\label{ssec:bias}

In \textsc{class\_sz} the fiducial first-order bias is the \cite{Tinker2010} formula:
\begin{equation}
    b^{(1)}(\nu)=1-A\frac{\nu^a}{\nu^a+\delta_c^a}+B\nu^b+C\nu^c\label{eq:b1tink}
\end{equation}
with parameters fixed to the values in Table \ref{tab:tinkerbias1}, which are from \cite{Tinker2010}.  It is a power-law at high-mass, flattens out at low-mass and is 1 at $\nu=0$. Recall, $\nu=\delta_c/\sigma(m)$ with $\sigma(m)$ from Eq.~\eqref{eq:sig2}.


We compute the second-order bias $b^{(2)}$ with the peak background split formula using Eq.~(8) of \cite{10.1093/mnras/stv702}, which follows \cite{Scoccimarro:2000gm}. Namely,

\begin{equation}
    b_2(\nu) = 2 (1+a_2)(\epsilon_1+E_1)+\epsilon_2+E_2\label{eq:b2pbs}
\end{equation}
where $a_2=-17/21$ is from the spherical collapse model and where $\epsilon_i$'s and $E_i$'s are computed from the \cite{Tinker2010} HMF parameters (see Table \ref{tab:HMFparams}) as given in Table \ref{tab:b2}. See also \cite{phils2020} for details on higher order biases.


