\subsection{Angular Power Spectra}\label{ss:autospec}



With the Limber approximation in flat-sky \citep[e.g., Appendix A of  ][and references therein]{HillPajer2013}, angular anisotropy power spectra are obtained by integrating the 3D power spectra, evaluated at $k_\ell=(\ell+1/2)/\chi$, over comoving volume 
\begin{equation}
    C_\ell^{XY}=\int\mathrm{d}\mathrm{v}  W^X(\chi)W^Y(\chi)P_{XY}^\mathrm{hm}\left(k_\ell,z\right)\label{eq:clxy}
\end{equation}
where $W^X$ and $W^Y$ are redshift dependent projection kernels (see Eq.~\ref{eq:zint}). Here, $P_{XY}^\mathrm{hm}$ is the 3d power spectrum of tracers $X$ and $Y$ evaluated in the halo model (see \ref{ss:ps}). 

