where the rate constants uniquely determine the rate form from the mass-action system \eqref{EnvZOmpr-simplified2-de}. In accordance with steps 1–3 of Definition \ref{def:xreduced}, we split the reaction $X_5 \stackrel{k_6}{\longrightarrow} X_2 + X_3$ into $X_5 \stackrel{k_6}{\longrightarrow} X_2$ and $X_5 \stackrel{k_6}{\longrightarrow} X_3$ to obtain the following $\mathcal{X}$-reduced interaction network $G_{\mathcal{X}} = (V_{\mathcal{X}},E_{\mathcal{X}})$ and potential splittings:
