    \label{fig:waveguide_barrier}
\end{figure}
Let the total field satisfy Neumann boundary conditions on \RED{the} waveguide walls, and on the strip. The total field is presented as the sum of the incident and scattered fields:
\[
u = u^{\rm sc} + u^{\rm in},\quad u^{\rm in}  = \exp\{-ik\cos\theta^{\rm in}x\}\cos(k\sin\theta^{\rm in}y), 
\]
\RED{The incident angle} $\theta^{\rm in}$ is \RED{a} Brillouin partial angle of a guided wave \RED{defined for some $n\in \mathbb{Z}$ chosen such that \green{$|\pi n/kb|\leq 1$} by}
\[
\sin\theta^{\rm in} = \frac{\pi n}{k b}.
\]
Using \RED{a} symmetry argument, one can show that 
\[u^{\rm sc}(y,0)=0 \text{ \ for \ } y\in (-h+a,0).\]
\RED{Therefore,} only the right half of the waveguide needs to be considered.

