 s e^{x_1} &\weq \la_2 + 2 \la_3 x_1 e^{x_1^2}, \\
 s e^{x_2} &\weq \la_2 + 2 \la_3 x_2 e^{x_2^2}.
\end{align*}
Define $u(t) = e^{s t} - \la_1 - \la_2 t - \la_3 e^{t^2}$.  Then the above conditions are equivalent to
$u(x_1)=0$, $u(x_2)=0$, $u'(x_1)=0$, $u'(x_2)=0$.

